  "body": "I decided to look at spec and find out how does UAs realize their own event loop. I found this https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model\r\n\r\nI've tryed to find steps about recalculate styles and so on, but I've not. \r\nWhy do I ask about it? Recently I decide to rewatch Jake Archibald video's \"in the Loop\". And the most interesting part of that video was part about rendering in UA. Of course Jake's diargramm is simplified, but still we can see stages of rendering like rAF then calculation styles then layout and finally painting. But if we consider that algorithm what I've pointed before. We only can see steps about rAF and painting. So main question is where are steps about calculation style and layout? Where do I should find them?\r\n\r\nAlso I have confusion about next demo: https://jsfiddle.net/o0eL47dc/\r\nBehaviour between chrome and firefox are different. And I try to figure out who from them is correct and why.\r\nIn generally, I need a clarification \r\nP.S I suspect that firefox is correct, because before painting it requires to complete rAF and then others calculations (styles, layout and so on)",
